1
00:00:04,175 --> 00:00:08,868
Whiskers and Luna's World. Episode two. The Seven Continents!

2
00:00:15,852 --> 00:00:19,677
One rainy morning, Luna was spinning her old globe.

3
00:00:19,877 --> 00:00:23,742
Luna, what are those colourful blobs on your globe? Sweets?

4
00:00:23,942 --> 00:00:28,091
They're not sweets, Whiskers! The big pieces of land are called continents.

5
00:00:28,291 --> 00:00:30,732
Continents? Is that a kind of cheese?

6
00:00:34,064 --> 00:00:36,000
How many continents are there, Luna?

7
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:39,239
Seven! Let's fly to them all. Hold on to the cushion!

8
00:00:48,833 --> 00:00:51,027
Whoosh! Up into the magic map!

9
00:00:56,967 --> 00:00:59,087
Look! Each colour is one continent.

10
00:01:10,768 --> 00:01:14,258
Ahoy, little flyers! I'm Albert the albatross.

11
00:01:14,458 --> 00:01:19,398
I have the longest wings of any bird. I glide over the oceans for miles and miles!

12
00:01:19,598 --> 00:01:22,487
Albert, how can we remember all seven continents?

13
00:01:22,687 --> 00:01:27,602
Easy! Sing along! Four A's: Africa, Antarctica, Asia, Australia.

14
00:01:27,802 --> 00:01:30,440
Two Americas, North and South.

15
00:01:30,640 --> 00:01:33,126
And Europe! That makes seven!

16
00:01:33,326 --> 00:01:37,282
Four, two, one... four hundred and twenty one continents!

17
00:01:37,482 --> 00:01:40,297
No, silly! Four plus two plus one makes seven!

18
00:01:43,629 --> 00:01:45,585
Follow me! Off we go!

19
00:01:57,789 --> 00:02:01,179
First, Europe. That's where we live! Remember the Eiffel Tower?

20
00:02:01,379 --> 00:02:03,186
Home of the finest cats!

21
00:02:09,127 --> 00:02:14,089
Africa! Lions and elephants live here. And look, the pyramids of Egypt!

22
00:02:22,117 --> 00:02:25,127
Asia! It's the biggest continent of all.

23
00:02:31,590 --> 00:02:33,870
It's huge! Who's that, munching bamboo?

24
00:02:34,070 --> 00:02:36,777
A giant panda! And the Great Wall of China.

25
00:02:42,718 --> 00:02:46,901
Australia! Kangaroos hop here, with babies in their pouches.

26
00:02:47,101 --> 00:02:50,404
A pocket for babies? I'd use it for snacks.

27
00:02:59,476 --> 00:03:03,126
Next stop, the bottom of the world: Antarctica!

28
00:03:03,326 --> 00:03:07,827
The bottom of the world? A warm, sunny beach! Sunglasses on!

29
00:03:21,074 --> 00:03:24,303
B-b-b-brr! Where's the b-b-beach?

30
00:03:24,503 --> 00:03:29,589
Ha ha! Antarctica is the coldest place on Earth, all covered in thick ice!

31
00:03:29,789 --> 00:03:33,177
Nobody lives here all year. Scientists only visit.

32
00:03:38,596 --> 00:03:40,134
But the penguins love it!

33
00:03:40,334 --> 00:03:43,614
I knew that. I froze on purpose. To stay fresh.

34
00:03:47,467 --> 00:03:50,287
Come on, frosty! Somewhere warmer!

35
00:04:01,446 --> 00:04:05,749
South America! The Amazon, the biggest rainforest in the world.

36
00:04:05,949 --> 00:04:08,060
And llamas, high up in the mountains!

37
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:18,233
North America! Bald eagles soar here, and big bison roam.

38
00:04:24,696 --> 00:04:26,974
Seven continents, all around the world!

39
00:04:27,174 --> 00:04:30,238
Now I'll glide home. Goodbye, friends!

40
00:04:37,744 --> 00:04:42,185
Remember! One. The Earth's land is split into seven continents.

41
00:04:44,733 --> 00:04:47,623
Two. Asia is the biggest continent.

42
00:04:50,172 --> 00:04:54,667
Three. Antarctica is the coldest continent, covered in ice.

43
00:05:00,607 --> 00:05:04,673
Quiz time! How many continents are there? Five, or seven?

44
00:05:08,266 --> 00:05:11,587
Seven! Four A's, two Americas, and Europe!

45
00:05:13,874 --> 00:05:18,803
Next. Which continent is the coldest? Africa, or Antarctica?

46
00:05:22,395 --> 00:05:25,245
Antarctica! Brrr! Well done!

47
00:05:32,229 --> 00:05:34,718
And with a twinkle, they were home.

48
00:05:34,918 --> 00:05:36,857
Seven continents in one day!

49
00:05:37,057 --> 00:05:40,198
Sure. But first, a nap. A nice, warm one.

50
00:05:44,051 --> 00:05:46,972
Next time, the five oceans! Goodnight!

